tool_calls.arguments:
{"code": "
tools = await nethack.nethack.list_tools()
for t in tools:
    print(t['name'], '-', t.get('description','')[:120])
"}

{"code": "
for t in tools:
    print(t['name'], '|', t.get('description',''))
    if 'inputSchema' in t:
        import json
        print('  schema:', json.dumps(t['inputSchema'], indent=2)[:300])
    print()
"}

message.content:
np_zap | Zap a wand in the given cardinal (n, e, s, w) or ordinal direction (ne, se, sw, nw) or target yourself using self.
  schema: {}

np_pickup | Pickup things at your location or specify where you want to pickup an item.
  schema: {}

np_up | Go up a staircase at your location or specify the position of the staircase you want to use.
  schema: {}

np_down | Go down a staircase at your location or specify the position of the staircase you want to use.
  schema: {}

np_loot | Loot a box on the floor.
  schema: {}

np_offer | Offer a sacrifice to the gods.
  schema: {}

np_drop | Drop an item.
  schema: {}

np_read | Read a scroll, spellbook, or something else.
  schema: {}

np_put_on | Put on an accessory.
  schema: {}

np_remove | Remove an accessory (ring, amulet, or blindfold).
  schema: {}

np_takeoff | Take off one piece of armor.
  schema: {}

np_wield | Wield a weapon.
  schema: {}

np_wear | Wear a piece of armor.
  schema: {}

np_apply | Apply (use) a tool. If used on a wand, that wand will be broken, releasing its magic in the process.
  schema: {}

np_eat | Eat something from your inventory or straight from the ground.
  schema: {}

np_drink | Drink something from your inventory or straight from the ground.
  schema: {}

np_tip | Tip out the content of a container.
  schema: {}

np_dip | Dip an object into something.
  schema: {}

np_kick | Kick something.
  schema: {}

np_rest | Rests n-moves while doing nothing or until something happens (default=5).
  schema: {}

np_cast | Opens your spellbook to cast a spell.
  schema: {}

np_pay | Pay your shopping bill.
  schema: {}

np_pray | Pray to the gods for help.
  schema: {}

np_look | Look at what is under you.
  schema: {}

np_set_avoid_monster_flag | If set to true skills will try to avoid monsters.
  schema: {}

np_melee_attack | Pursues and attacks a given target using melee attacks until it is dead.
  schema: {}

np_explore_level | Explores the level to find new rooms, as well as hidden doors and corridors.
  schema: {}

np_move_to | Move to the specified position using pathfinding.
  schema: {}

np_go_to | Moves to the specified room or corridor using the shortest path possible.
  schema: {}

np_press_key | Presses the given letter. For special keys only ESC, SPACE, and ENTER are supported.
  schema: {}

np_type_text | Types the text by pressing the keys in order.
  schema: {}

reveal | Reveal a rectangular region of the dungeon map as ASCII (for the bounding-box observation mode, where the map is otherwise hidden). Coordinates are map cells: x = column 0-78, y = row 0-20, inclusive. The FULL map (x1=0, y1=0, x2=78, y2=20) is a valid request and returns all 79 columns. Returns the sub-rectangle as text; consumes NO game turn. Out-of-range requests are clamped to the grid, and any clamping is stated in the reply.
  schema: {}

rollback | Undo the last n turns, returning the game to the state it was in before them. Use after a mistake -- walking into a losing fight, triggering a trap, wasting turns in a dead end. Costs one turn and no game time. n must be between 1 and 15.
  schema: {}

